  "outlook": "\u201cWhen we issued our 2017 outlook in February, we indicated that our quarterly earnings in Q1 would be the softest of the year. We also noted the recent uptick in orders, including the increase in U.S. industrial orders since December of last year. These trends continued through the end of the first quarter,\u201d Sherman noted. \u201cWhile it is still early days, the first quarter order improvement gives us confidence in our full-year outlook. At this time, we are reaffirming our full-year 2017 adjusted EPS outlook of $0.70 to $0.78.\u201d"
